    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21896" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενν-άδας</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ</span>, (
			Dor.
		 word) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>noble,
				generous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρηστὸς καὶ γ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					179
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. καὶ πρᾷος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					243c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1100b32
			</span></i>; <i>highly bred</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τῶν γενναδῶν ἵππων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Polem.Phgn.
					78
				</span></i>
			; <i>notable</i>, c. inf., <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				33
			</span></i>.</div>
